<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="text-align: right; margin: 0"><B>Exhibit 99.2</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="text-align: center; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"><IMG SRC="logo.jpg" ALT=""></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; margin: 0pt 0">ELECTRA BATTERY MATERIALS CORPORATION</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: center; margin: 0pt 0"><B>SPECIAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: center; margin: 0pt 0"><B>NOTICE-AND-ACCESS NOTIFICATION</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: center; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">You are receiving this notification because Electra Battery Materials Corporation
(the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;) has decided to use &ldquo;notice-and-access&rdquo; for delivery of proxy solicitation materials to
its shareholders for its special meeting of shareholders (the &ldquo;<B>Meeting</B>&rdquo;) to be held on Friday, December 20, 2024. Under
notice-and-access, shareholders still receive a proxy or voting instruction form enabling them to vote at the Meeting. However, instead
of a paper copy of the management information circular of the Company dated October 31, 2024 (the &ldquo;<B>Circular</B>&rdquo;), shareholders
receive this notice with information on how they may access the Circular electronically through a website and under the Company&rsquo;s
SEDAR+ profile. This process directly benefits the Company through a substantial reduction in both postage and material costs and also
helps the environment through a decrease in paper documents that are ultimately discarded. Under notice-and-access, proxy-related materials
will be available for viewing for up to one (1) year from the date of posting, and a paper copy of the Circular can be requested at any
time during this period.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">All shareholders are strongly encouraged to vote in advance of the Meeting
using the proxy form or the voting instruction form provided to them with the Circular. You are entitled to vote at the Meeting and any
postponement or adjournment thereof if you owned Common Shares (as defined below) at the close of business on the record date of October
31, 2024.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><U>MEETING DATE, TIME AND LOCATION</U>:</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B></B></P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="border-collapse: collapse; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%">
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left">
  <TD STYLE="width: 9%"><B>Date:</B></TD>
  <TD STYLE="width: 91%"><B>Friday, December 20, 2024</B></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left">
  <TD><B>&nbsp;</B></TD>
  <TD><B>&nbsp;</B></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left">
  <TD><B>Time:</B></TD>
  <TD><B>10:00 a.m. (Toronto time)</B></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left">
  <TD><B>&nbsp;</B></TD>
  <TD><B>&nbsp;</B></TD></TR>
<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left">
  <TD><B>Location:</B></TD>
  <TD><B>Cassels Brock &amp; Blackwell LLP, Suite 3200, Bay Adelaide Centre, &#9;North Tower, 40 Temperance Street, Toronto, Ontario,
  M5H 0B4</B></TD></TR>
</TABLE>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">THE FOLLOWING MATTERS, ALL AS MORE PARTICULARLY DESCRIBED IN THE CIRCULAR,
WILL BE REVIEWED AND VOTED ON AT THE MEETING:</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 5pt"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 36pt">1.</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">To consider and, if deemed advisable, to approve with or without variation, a special resolution authorizing
an amendment to the articles of the Company to complete a reverse stock split (the &ldquo;<B>Reverse Split</B>&rdquo;) of the issued and
outstanding common shares (the <B>&ldquo;Common Shares</B>&rdquo;) of the Company at a ratio of one (1) post-Reverse Split Common Share
for between three (3) to five (5) pre-Reverse Split Common Shares, as determined by the Board of Directors of the Company in its sole
discretion, if at all, and as more particularly described in the Circular;</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 5pt"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 36pt">2.</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">To consider and, if deemed advisable, to approve with or without variation, an ordinary resolution of
disinterested shareholders to approve the 2024 Employee Share Purchase Plan for the Company, as more particularly described in the Circular;
and</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 1 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 4pt solid"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"></P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="width: 5.05pt"></TD><TD STYLE="width: 36pt">3.</TD><TD STYLE="text-align: justify">To transact such further or other business as may properly come before the meeting or any adjournment
or adjournments thereof.</TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-weight: normal">For detailed information regarding each
of the above items of business, please refer to Part 2 of the Circular titled &ldquo;Business of the Meeting&rdquo;.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 5.05pt">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">SHAREHOLDERS ARE REMINDED TO <U>REVIEW</U> THE CIRCULAR
<U>PRIOR</U> TO VOTING. It is important that your Common Shares be represented at this Meeting to ensure a quorum is present. If you cannot
be present to vote in person, please ensure that your proxy or, if a corporation, your representative, is appointed and present to vote
on your behalf at the Meeting. Instructions regarding the appointment of a proxy or representative are contained in the Circular and in
the accompanying proxy or voting instruction form.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><U>WEBSITES WHERE THE MEETING MATERIALS ARE POSTED</U>:</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">The proxy-related materials for the Meeting may be viewed online at www.sedarplus.ca
under the profile of the Company, or at the following internet address:</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">https://www.electrabmc.com/investors/?scroll=agm.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><U>HOW TO OBTAIN PAPER COPIES OF THE CIRCULAR</U>:</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">If you wish to receive a paper copy of the Circular or have questions about
notice-and-access for the current Meeting, please call the Company&rsquo;s transfer agent, TSX Trust Company, at 1-888-433-6443 or by
email at tsxt-fulfilment@tmx.com. In order to receive a paper copy of the Circular in time to vote before the Meeting, your request should
be received at least five (5) business days in advance of the proxy deposit date and time set out in the accompanying proxy or voting
instruction form. If you do request the Circular, please note that another proxy or voting instruction form will not be sent to you; please
retain your current one enclosed for voting purposes. To obtain paper copies of the materials after the date of the Meeting, please contact
the Company by: (i) mail to 133 Richmond Street West, Suite 602, Toronto, Ontario, M5H 2L3; or (ii) e-mail to info@ElectraBMC.com.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">The Company will not use the procedure known as &ldquo;stratification&rdquo;
in relation to the use of notice-and-access provisions. Stratification occurs when a reporting issuer using the notice-and-access provisions
provides a paper copy of the Circular to certain shareholders with the notice package.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><U>HOW TO VOTE YOUR COMMON SHARES</U>:</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">Please follow the instructions accompanying the proxy or voting instruction
form you received, and kindly ensure that you return your proxy no later than 10:00 a.m. (Toronto time) on Wednesday, December 18, 2024.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><B>YOU CANNOT VOTE BY RETURNING THIS NOTICE</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">Registered shareholders can vote in person as noted above and by proxy
in one of the following ways:</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in"><B>Internet</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in">Go to www.meeting-vote.com and follow the instructions on the
screen. You will need your control number, which appears below your name and address on the proxy form.</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 4pt solid"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B></B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B>Fax and Email</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">Complete both sides of the proxy form, sign and date it and fax
both sides to the Company&rsquo;s transfer agent, TSX Trust Company, Attention: Proxy Department, to 416-595-9593 or scan and email to
proxyvote@tmx.com.</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B>Mail</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in">Complete, sign and date the proxy form and return it in the envelope
provided, or send it to: TSX Trust, Attention: Proxy Department, P.O. Box 721, Agincourt, Ontario, M1S 0A1, Canada.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">Non-registered shareholders are asked to return their voting instructions
using the methods set out on their voting instruction form or business reply envelope well in advance of the proxy deposit date noted
on your voting instruction form.</P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0pt 0; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Shareholders with questions about notice-and-access generally can call
toll-free at 1-888-433-6443. </B>Terms used but not otherwise defined herein have the meanings ascribed thereto in the Circular.</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">Dated at Toronto, Ontario, on October 31, 2024.</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0">On Behalf of the Board of Directors</P>

<P STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0"><I>&ldquo;Trent Mell&rdquo;</I></P>

